.TH "SOPLOS-WEBAPP-MANAGER" "1" "2026-10-19" "Soplos Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
soplos-webapp-manager \- Create and manage isolated Web Applications for Soplos Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B soplos-webapp-manager
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B soplos-webapp-manager
is the official Site Specific Browser (SSB) manager for Soplos Linux.
Built with Tauri 2, Rust, and Svelte architecture, it turns any website into
its own desktop application with an isolated browser profile:
.IP \[bu] 2
Create a WebApp from any URL, with its own isolated browser profile and
desktop entry.
.IP \[bu]
Works with whichever supported browser you already have installed: Firefox,
LibreWolf, Zen Browser, Midori, Chromium, Google Chrome, Brave, Brave Origin,
Vivaldi, Opera, Opera GX, Microsoft Edge, Helium or GNOME Web, native or
Flatpak.
.IP \[bu]
Drag a link from the browser's address bar onto the window to create a
WebApp from it directly.
.IP \[bu]
Automatic favicon lookup, or pick your own icon.
.IP \[bu]
Every section of the application menu as a category, changeable when
editing.
.IP \[bu]
Extensions for each WebApp. With Firefox-based browsers they are searched in
addons.mozilla.org from the form, or added from an .xpi file, and installed in
the profile of the WebApp. With browsers based on Chrome, a button opens the
extension store of the browser with the profile of the WebApp.
.IP \[bu]
Optional navigation bar, incognito mode and extra browser launch parameters
per WebApp. For browsers based on Chrome the common parameters are
checkboxes linked with the text field.
.IP \[bu]
Edit or delete any WebApp at any time; deleting removes its desktop entry
and its isolated profile.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show summary of options.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B F1
About dialog.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
Add a new WebApp.
.TP
.B Delete
Remove the selected WebApp.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit the application.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/soplos-webapp-*.desktop
Desktop entries created for each WebApp.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/soplos-webapps/<id>/
Isolated browser profile directory for each WebApp.
